# ============================================================
# host_login-1  (also applies to host_login-2 and host_login-3)
# Role : end host in the VXLAN segment
# Image: busybox / Alpine (Part 1 host image)
# eth0 : connected to its local VTEP's br0 bridge port
# ============================================================

# No IP address is assigned by default (subject requirement).
# During testing you can assign one manually:
#
#   ip addr add 20.1.1.1/24 dev eth0   (host_login-1)
#   ip addr add 20.1.1.2/24 dev eth0   (host_login-2)
#   ip addr add 20.1.1.3/24 dev eth0   (host_login-3)
#
# After assignment the VTEPs will automatically discover
# the MACs via BGP EVPN type-2 routes (no flooding needed
# because nolearning + advertise-all-vni are set on VTEPs).

# ============================================================
# Address plan summary (P3)
# ============================================================
#
# Loopbacks (VTEP tunnel endpoints):
#   1.1.1.1/32  _login-1  (RR)
#   1.1.1.2/32  _login-2  (VTEP)
#   1.1.1.3/32  _login-3  (VTEP)
#   1.1.1.4/32  _login-4  (VTEP)
#
# Underlay point-to-point links (OSPF area 0):
#   10.1.1.0/30   _login-1 (.1) <-> _login-2 (.2)
#   10.1.1.4/30   _login-1 (.5) <-> _login-3 (.6)
#   10.1.1.8/30   _login-1 (.9) <-> _login-4 (.10)
#
# Overlay (VXLAN VNI 10 / bridge br0):
#   20.1.1.0/24   host segment (optional IPs for ping test)
#   20.1.1.1      host_login-1
#   20.1.1.2      host_login-2
#   20.1.1.3      host_login-3

# ============================================================
# Expected BGP EVPN route types
# ============================================================
# Type 3 (IMET / Inclusive Multicast Ethernet Tag):
#   - Advertised automatically by each VTEP when VXLAN is up.
#   - Tells other VTEPs "I am reachable at this tunnel IP for VNI 10".
#   - Present BEFORE any host comes up.
#
# Type 2 (MAC/IP Advertisement):
#   - Advertised when a host's MAC appears on a VTEP's bridge.
#   - Created AUTOMATICALLY – no IP assignment needed.
#   - Allows remote VTEPs to install a forwarding entry
#     pointing to the originating VTEP.
